From b6e4a74552c9b77a1993a09ba6eab443ec25f5ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian <219239532+markd3ng@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 16:43:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(mpu): keep password, uploadId, and key out of query
 strings

Context:
D-SEC-003 / Issue #76. MPU create-update, resume, complete, and abort
put the paste management password and/or R2 key and uploadId in the URL
query string, so those values appear in access logs, Referer, and
browser history.

Expected behavior:
New official clients send X-PB-Password, X-PB-MPU-Key, and
X-PB-MPU-Upload-Id. Query password/key/uploadId are accepted only as
backward-compat fallback when the matching header is absent. Header
wins if both are present. partNumber and public paste name may stay in
the query. Worker warn logs no longer interpolate those secrets.
Knowledge-of-(key, uploadId) remains MPU session auth.

Acceptance criteria:
- uploadMPU create-update, resume, complete, and abort URLs have no
  password, uploadId, or key query params
- header-only Worker create-update, resume, and abort succeed
- query-only old clients still work
- header wins over a conflicting query password
- docs describe headers, fallback, and residual threat

Constraints:
- generic upstream patch only; no Feishu conditionals
- no Durable Object / lease / new ownership record
- do not modify upstream-sync
- no Codex retry while quota remains exhausted

Validation:
- TDD RED: shared/test/uploadPaste.spec.ts failed because uploadMPU still
  put password/uploadId/key in the query (3 failed, 9 passed)
- GREEN: shared/test/uploadPaste.spec.ts worker/test/mpuErrors.spec.ts
  worker/test/mpu.spec.ts -> 3 files, 29 passed
- REGRESSION: Node v22.23.2 / pnpm 10.28.0 vitest run --testTimeout 15000
  -> 21 files, 159 tests passed
- pnpm lint PASS; pnpm typecheck PASS; prettier -c on changed files PASS
- pnpm build:frontend PASS

